node_modules

# Raw source media — the large camera/editor originals. These live ONLY at the
# repo root and are never served; scripts/encode-video.mjs and to-webp.mjs turn
# them into the delivery files under public/.
#
# The leading slash matters. Unanchored `assets/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed public/assets/ — the processed
# WebP images the site actually loads. Likewise a blanket `*.mp4` / `*.webm`
# stripped public/video/*, so the encoded clips 404'd on deploy while working
# locally. Anchor to the root; do not re-add extension globs here.
/assets/
